The concept of a Lie derivative is introduced in order to quantify how tensors change along some given “direction” in the manifold, specified by a vector field X. Contrary to the covariant derivative, it will be seen that the Lie derivative does not change the order of the tensor it differentiates.
D.1. Lie derivative of a function, i. e., a scalar
